    "ART_PROMPT": "A figure formed of red clay earth rising from the dusty ground, silhouetted against a primitive garden landscape, warm earthy tones, rough texture, no text.",
    "ABILITY_TEXT": "Look at the top 3 cards of the Tower; return them in any order.",
    "STAT_LORE": 5,
    "STAT_CONTEXT": 5,
    "STAT_COMPLEXITY": 2,
    "OT_VERSE_REF": "Genesis 2:7",
    "OT_VERSE_SNIPPET": "And the LORD God formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life.",
    "NT_VERSE_REF": "John 19:5",
    "NT_VERSE_SNIPPET": "Then came Jesus forth, wearing the crown of thorns... And Pilate saith unto them, Behold the man!",
    "OT_VERSE_LINE": "Genesis 2:7 — “And the LORD God formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life.”",
    "NT_VERSE_LINE": "John 19:5 — “Then came Jesus forth, wearing the crown of thorns... And Pilate saith unto them, Behold the man!”",
    "GREEK": "ἄνθρωπος",
    "GREEK_TRANSLIT": "anthrōpos",
    "HEBREW": "אָדָם",
